#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:3
#: 8d1539576fd24cad8c36d790b2700a89
msgid "How to use the hardware compatibility list (HCL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:6
#: 25e3c5c3d3544c099cd528581fc20eb5
msgid ""
"The `HCL <https://www.qubes-os.org/hcl/>`__ is a compilation of reports "
"generated and submitted by users across various Qubes versions about their "
"hardware’s compatibility with Qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:9
#: 6707d3f9de774af3891c128340c43911
msgid ""
"Raw HCL data is available on `github <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"hcl>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:12
#: f996c987bff94bdeb72f786e84f1f4b9
msgid ""
"Except in the case of developer-reported entries, the Qubes team has not "
"independently verified the accuracy of these reports. Please first consult "
"the data sheets (CPU, chipset, motherboard) prior to buying new hardware for "
"Qubes. Make sure it meets the :doc:`System Requirements </user/hardware/"
"system-requirements>` and search in particular for support of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:14
#: 272a44d5a9e44b9f98cc7a046edf1a03
msgid ""
"HVM (“AMD virtualization (AMD-V)”, “Intel virtualization (VT-x)”, “VIA "
"virtualization (VIA VT)”)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:16
#: 02a1d0d0eaf544c79aced84c72ddae15
msgid ""
"IOMMU (“AMD I/O Virtualization Technology (AMD-Vi)”, “Intel Virtualization "
"Technology for Directed I/O (VT-d)”)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:18
#: b7de026c571e4f7dabd095ed605387c0
msgid ""
"TPM (“Trusted Platform Module (TPM)” connected to a “20-pin TPM header” on "
"motherboards.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:22
#: fc9acfe67cfd4741b5556f6bb3399742
msgid ""
"If using the list to make a purchasing decision, we recommend that you "
"choose hardware with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:24
#: ed1cda1327b84fb7b3ae8cd7f16242a7
msgid ""
"the best achievable Qubes security level (green columns in HVM, IOMMU, TPM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:26
#: 38bde52847934112a05ac2c73e05d059
msgid ""
"and general machine compatibility (green columns in Qubes version, dom0 "
"kernel, remarks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:30
#: 28e8073c92f246a2ba55fd53c2ec1890
msgid ""
"Also see :doc:`Certified Hardware </user/hardware/certified-hardware/"
"certified-hardware>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:33
#: 76a2c9c1e63b4af9ae014fe8e75f7c67
msgid "Generating and Submitting New Reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:36
#: d4a536fd5dcf414988a8ed4bbcf8c1a1
msgid ""
"In order to generate an HCL report in Qubes, simply open a terminal in dom0 "
"(Applications Menu > Terminal Emulator) and run ``qubes-hcl-report <qube-"
"name>``, where ``<qube-name>`` is the name of the qube in which the "
"generated HCL files will be saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:38
#: 4354e11207274ab8a0fb93f9c4603c5d
msgid ""
"You are encouraged to submit your HCL report for the benefit of further "
"Qubes development and other users. When submitting reports, test the "
"hardware yourself, if possible. If you would like to submit your HCL report, "
"please copy and paste the contents of the **HCL Info** ``.yml`` file into an "
"email to the :ref:`qubes-users mailing list <introduction/support:qubes-"
"users>` with the subject ``HCL - <your machine model name>``, or create a "
"post in the `HCL Reports category <https://forum.qubes-os.org/c/user-support/"
"hcl-reports/23>`__ of the forum. Pasting the contents into the email or post "
"has the advantage that members of the mailing list and the forum can see the "
"report without downloading and opening a file. In addition, new forum "
"members are unable to attach files to posts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:40
#: 0ed63e317bd04a2d8aab770a62198e3b
msgid ""
"Please include any useful information about any Qubes features you may have "
"tested (see the legend below), as well as general machine compatibility "
"(video, networking, sleep, etc.). Please consider sending the **HCL Support "
"Files** ``.cpio.gz`` file as well. To generate these add the ``-s`` or ``--"
"support`` command line option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/hardware/how-to-use-the-hcl.rst:43
#: 04de99710e67420f9ff4288f85b43bdc
msgid ""
"The **HCL Support Files** may contain numerous hardware details, including "
"serial numbers. If, for privacy or security reasons, you do not wish to make "
"this information public, please **do not** post the ``.cpio.gz`` file on a "
"public mailing list or forum."
msgstr ""
